// When an enum constructor and a global class have the same name, a bare
// pattern name is a tag test, not a class test
// (spec/04-semantics.md, match Expression, "Constructor patterns"). The
// class `Foo` replaces the global `Foo` after the enum is declared, but the
// pattern was fixed as a tag test when the match was compiled.
enum E { Foo Bar }
var e = Bar();
class Foo {}

print match e {
    case Foo => "foo"
    case Bar => "bar"
};

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: bar
